    <blockquote>
    <h2>v6.4.1</h2>
    <h3>Patch Changes</h3>
    <ul>
    <li><a
    href="https://redirect.github.com/enisdenjo/graphql-ws/pull/703">#703</a>
    <a
    href="https://github.com/enisdenjo/graphql-ws/commit/707c38cbf7bad4fefd21d276cbabcce079606522"><code>707c38c</code></a>
    Thanks <a href="https://github.com/lprnmns"><code>@​lprnmns</code></a>!
    - Use the <code>jsonMessageReplacer</code> when automatically responding
    to a ping with a pong, on both the client and the server</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>v6.4.0</h2>
    <h3>Minor Changes</h3>
    <ul>
    <li><a
    href="https://redirect.github.com/enisdenjo/graphql-ws/pull/696">#696</a>
    <a
    href="https://github.com/enisdenjo/graphql-ws/commit/83be0521d510e3d53ee61288fda0f57dcfee78af"><code>83be052</code></a>
    Thanks <a
    href="https://github.com/niukanen1"><code>@​niukanen1</code></a>! - Add
    an <code>isProd</code> option to the <code>ws</code>,
    <code>uWebSockets.js</code> and <code>@fastify/websocket</code>
    use-server helpers, matching the existing <code>crossws</code> option.
    It controls whether internal error messages are masked with
    <code>Internal server error</code> before reaching the client,
    defaulting to the <code>NODE_ENV === 'production'</code> check as
    before. This lets apps running in production keep reporting
    <code>onConnect</code> error messages to the client by opting out, or
    mask eagerly in non-production environments.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Patch Changes</h3>
    <ul>
    <li>
    <p><a
    href="https://redirect.github.com/enisdenjo/graphql-ws/pull/700">#700</a>
    <a
    href="https://github.com/enisdenjo/graphql-ws/commit/d8aeda6504268e8b6a74e49c128393b9617a0ed5"><code>d8aeda6</code></a>
    Thanks <a href="https://github.com/kratam"><code>@​kratam</code></a>! -
    Fix the client closing an in-use socket when many subscriptions complete
    at once and a new one subscribes within the
    <code>lazyCloseTimeout</code></p>
    <p>Every completing subscription scheduled its own lazy close timeout,
    but only the last one got cleared on the next connect. The client now
    keeps a single lazy close timeout and checks for active subscriptions
    before closing.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
    <p><a
    href="https://redirect.github.com/enisdenjo/graphql-ws/pull/702">#702</a>
    <a
    href="https://github.com/enisdenjo/graphql-ws/commit/1e05c8c2e6701d006b0e09c849dfadc234a79f4c"><code>1e05c8c</code></a>
    Thanks <a href="https://github.com/Meemaw"><code>@​Meemaw</code></a>! -
    Avoid an unhandled rejection when a subscription is disposed before the
    connection is acknowledged and the socket closes before the subscription
    releases its connection lock (for example, when the client is disposed
    while connecting and the WebSocket implementation delivers the close
    event on a microtask).</p>
    </li>
    </ul>
    <h2>v6.3.0</h2>
    <h3>Minor Changes</h3>
    <ul>
    <li><a
    href="https://redirect.github.com/enisdenjo/graphql-ws/pull/691">#691</a>
    <a
    href="https://github.com/enisdenjo/graphql-ws/commit/b5f53cd4c051130b43fdb8df936d0cfdb489f084"><code>b5f53cd</code></a>
    Thanks <a
    href="https://github.com/niukanen1"><code>@​niukanen1</code></a>! - Add
    <code>onPing</code> and <code>onPong</code> server callbacks to
    <code>ServerOptions</code>, similar to <code>onConnect</code> and
    <code>onDisconnect</code>. The callbacks receive the connection
    <code>Context</code> as the first argument and the ping/pong
    <code>payload</code> as the second, allowing apps to log or react to
    subprotocol-level pings with access to connection state. The automatic
    pong reply is preserved when using the server-level <code>onPing</code>
    callback; the low-level websocket <code>onPing</code> listener still
    disables the automatic reply for full manual control.</li>
    </ul>
